[Start "danish-gambit-declined 2...exd4"]

3. Qxd4 { White recaptures with the queen. It will be chased away, which costs White time. } 3... Nc6 { Develops with an attack on the queen. } 4. Qe3 ( 4. Qd1 { The queen goes home, but White has spent two moves on it and has nothing developed. } 4... Nf6 5. Nc3 ( 5. Bd3 d5 { Opens the centre while White's king is still on e1. } ) 5... Bb4 ) ( 4. Qc4 Nf6 5. Nc3 Bb4 ) ( 4. Qd5 Nf6 ) ( 4. Qa4 Nf6 5. Nc3 Bb4 ) ( 4. Qd3 Nf6 5. Nc3 Bb4 ) 4... Nf6 { Develops with an attack on e4. The queen must now guard that pawn, and on e3 it blocks its own bishop. } 5. Nc3 ( 5. Bb5 a6 { Asks the bishop at once. After Bxc6 dxc6 Black has the two bishops and open lines. } 6. Bxc6 dxc6 ) ( 5. Nf3 Be7 ) ( 5. e5 Ng4 { The knight attacks the queen and the pawn on e5 together. } 6. Qe4 ( 6. Qe2 d6 ) 6... Ngxe5 { Takes the pawn with the knight. If f4, ...d5 hits the queen and Black's pieces come out with gains of time. } 7. f4 d5 ) 5... Bb4 { Pins the knight to the king. There is no pawn on d2, so the bishop on b4 looks straight at the king. } 6. Bd2 O-O { Gets the king out of the middle. } 7. O-O-O Re8 { Puts the rook on the e-file, where it pressures e4 and the queen. } 8. Bc4 d6 { Opens the c8 bishop and covers e5. Plan: ...Bg4 or ...Be6 to trade White's bishop, with the rook on e8 ready to punish any careless move that leaves e4 loose. } *
